## 5. UX patterns (Medicare.gov + Senior Planet)

- **Action-first:** “What do you want to do / check?”
- Large **task cards** with plain verbs: Find, Get, Check, See, Open, Compare, Try again
- One job per section; short help line under titles
- Calm hierarchy; help path obvious; no clutter
- Soft borders, generous whitespace, minimal chrome
- Prefer plain English over jargon (`Discount` not `P/D`; `Income rate` not `Dist`; `Borrowing` not `Lev`)
- Error/loading copy a non-developer can understand

```css
.gy-task-card {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: flex-start;
  gap: 0.5rem;
  min-height: 5.5rem;
  padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
  border-radius: 0.75rem;
  border: 1px solid var(--gy-border);
  background: var(--gy-surface);
  text-align: left;
}
.gy-task-card[data-active="true"],
.gy-task-card[aria-pressed="true"] {
  border-color: var(--gy-blue);
  background: var(--gy-blue-soft);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--gy-blue);
}
```

